<title>HONG KONG: China plans to issue 1.07 bln yuan power bonds.</title>
<headline>China plans to issue 1.07 bln yuan power bonds.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's Ministry of Power Industry is planning to make a public offer of 1.0752 billion yuan worth of bonds to domestic investors this year, an official of the ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He told the Hong Kong-based newsletter China Securities Bulletin that the issue required approval from the State Planning Commission and the People's Bank of China.</p>
<p>If the issue is approved, the ministry will use the money raised from the bonds for 12 major power plants, classified by the state as key electric power projects and including one in the Inner Mongolia region, he said.</p>
<p>He gave no more details.</p>
</text>
